+// GameNative: every game in a session gets ONE uniform app id, regardless of
+// the store it came from (Steam/GOG/Epic/custom). Without --steam, gamescope
+// otherwise derives w->appID from the Xwayland window id (map_win/add_win
+// below) -- a per-launch value the app process cannot know, since the
+// gamescope_control client that calls request_app_performance_stats() lives in
+// the app process with no X11 connection. The requested id keys
+// wlserver.app_perf_requests, which wlserver_app_presented() matches against
+// w->appID (published on the base plane); a fixed id makes both sides agree
+// with no cross-process channel and no file I/O. The app side (GameNative
+// GameNativeDrm.GAMESCOPE_APP_ID) must use the same value.
+static constexpr uint32_t kGameNativeUniformAppId = 1;
+
 #define TRANSLUCENT	0x00000000
 #define OPAQUE		0xffffffff
 
